    "lawSection": "Real Property",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4975A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to authorize to Living Water for Women, Inc. to\nfile an application for a real property tax exemption\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation would allow a retroactive application for real\nproperty tax exemption for Living Water for Women Inc.. for property\nowned in the City of Glen Cove.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill would authorize the assessor of the City of Glen\nCove to accept an application for an exemption from real property\ntaxes as if made pursuant to § 420-a of the Real Property Tax Law. If\nsatisfied that the Living Water for Women Inc. would otherwise have\nbeen entitled to said exemption, the assessor, upon approval of the\ncity council may, in his or her sole discretion, provide for a refund\nor cancel all remaining unpaid taxes, interest, related fines and\npenalties.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nLiving Water's mission is to help formerly incarcerated women so that\nthey may become vital members of the community. Living Water for\nWomen's goal is to establish a structured transitional home for women\nwho have been incarcerated in the Nassau County Jail.  It is intended\nby this bill to ameliorate the hardship that will be suffered by the\nLiving Water for Women Inc., a charitable entity under § 420-a of the\nReal Property Tax Law, if it is required to pay the property taxes due\nas described above.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
